    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>When a layer requests and authentication, this handler is triggered. When the credentials are found in QgsCredentials (because it&apos;s stored before), they are used for the login. If not, QGIS would popup a Login Dialog, but QField does not. The realms (where it should log in to) are just added to the list of unhandled realms. When all layers are handled, the login dialog is diplayed for each of them. On successful login, the credentials are stored in QgsCredentials and removed from the list. When the list is empty (or contains only canceled realms), the project is reloaded. This time the logins are contained in QgsCredentials and no dialog needs to pop up. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
